<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dalta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 708 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dalta was a king of Ellipi, a kingdom in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the late 8th century BCE. A loyal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a>, he was restored by Assyrian troops after a rebellion, and the rebels of Harhar turned to him against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>. His death in 708 BCE led to a succession war between his sons Nibe, supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishpabara">Ishpabara</a>, backed by Assyria.</p></div>
